"Proposal written to /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-liammagnier-Developer-project-juno/bfdee244-0283-4629-a3f4-3c603fc89908/scratchpad/merge/proposal-object-first.md (about 20k words, sections 0\u201314, 6 ASCII wireframes, all 101 R-ids and X-01 to X-33 placed).\n1. Thesis: an artifact is a file with an id, owner, home, versions and a canonical `/a/{id}`. No chat gesture can delete it; edit and regenerate make branches (\"Try 2\") and chat delete detaches it (X-03/X-04/X-22).\n2. Every artifact has a thread: the made-in chat for the owner, plus a lazy private `ArtifactThread` per collaborator, so sharing never leaks anyone's chat. Comments sent to Juno become turns and the reply comes back to the comment.\n3. Conversation left, object right at every size: card, panel, full window, public page, iPhone sheet, Mac TrailingDock and document window. One `ArtifactSurface` mounted by artifact id; a version is data, never a key (the X-02 law).\n4. Expand (\u2318\u21e7\u21a9) uses `pushState` to `/a/{id}`: the transcript folds into a leading Chat pane, the composer moves with its draft, and Back restores the chat. A direct load renders the same layout.\n5. The library is the spine: one Artifacts row with posters, server search, scopes, sort, trash and a New menu that creates the object first (no holder chat). Design becomes a kind, a filter and a New item; `/design` and `/design/{id}` redirect, 307 then 308.\n6. Registry (`artifact-kinds.ts`, generated to Swift and OpenAPI): Design, Deck, Doc, Page, Code, Diagram, Graphic, Image, Sheet, Design system, File, each with editor, runtime, poster, exports, comment anchor, roles and phone contract.\n7. Data: `Artifact.userId`/`projectId`/`deletedAt`, nullable `conversationId` (SetNull), `messageId` renamed in code only via `@map`, version provenance, a working head that seals into versions, plus comments, grants, proposals, pins and pinned `Share.versionId`.\n8. Critical finding: the sync change trigger finds an artifact's owner through its conversation (`migration 20260815180000:52-54`). Detaching without first rewriting it to use `Artifact.userId` silently removes artifacts from every device.\n9. Ship order: tolerant native build first (ported to main, not held for the full glass release), then additive schema, owner-by-userId triggers, no-delete behaviour, contract. New sync entities and kinds are gated per account on client builds seen in 30 days.\n10. AI loop: Juno reads a digest of the current version plus the selection and emits create, patch (exact anchors) or design ops. Every change is a proposal card in the thread; people's edits win; big changes land on a branch in Compare; Ask Juno merges into chat.\n11. Share = live grants (viewer, commenter, editor); Publish = snapshot pinned to a version with Update and Unpublish on the same URL. The X-01 fix ships in two gates: private previews first, scripted public pages only after suspend, takedown, report, screening, rate limits and `connect-src 'self'`.\n12. Figma-grade push where the engine is strong: layout fixes, on-canvas handles, live components, variables everywhere, motion v2, one runtime with conformance tests, Play and Present, Inspect. Hold vector networks, boolean ops and live cursors.\n13. Work deliverables: index them under \"From tasks\" now and persist the spec; in Phase 5 they become typed Doc, Deck, Sheet and File artifacts over the same stored bytes. Office and PDF become validated exports of a version, with one OOXML renderer.\n14. Roadmap: P0 stop the bleeding, P1 the object, P2 one surface, P3 Juno in the object, P4 together, P5 typed kinds, plus a parallel editor track. Each phase has exit tests, flags, rollback and a must-not-ship-before table; 18 owner decisions carry recommended answers."